{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1510760-reworking-monster-powers-for-cofd-blue-book-core","id":1510760,"title":"Reworking Monster Powers for CofD Blue Book/Core?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-05-04T23:56:19-07:00","id":1510760,"title":"Reworking Monster Powers for CofD Blue Book/Core?","content":"Probably sounds like a ridiculous thing to do but let me explain\u2026<br /> <br /> So for starters I should probably explain why I\u2019m running a core chronicle.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>my players are all mortals</li> <li>existence of the supernatural is going to be revealed over the course of the chronicle</li> <li>mortal threats take precedence over supernatural ones</li> <li>thematically it makes more sense</li> </ol>But I allowed my players, if they wanted, to have superpowers. My main reason for this is because I felt like there should be some ostracized group that the current government scapegoated during their rise to power. I didn\u2019t want to have the government single out a specific race or ethnicity because that\u2019s racist &amp; I\u2019m not about that. (<i>Also my players are all white &amp; playing white characters so it wouldn\u2019t work thematically w/ such a group.</i>) I didn\u2019t go with the idea of supernaturals being the target because again I\u2019m planning to have that be revealed over time.<br /> <br /> I know you\u2019re probably wondering &quot;why don\u2019t you run a DtR chronicle?&quot; Well to be honest it has a lot going on that I just don\u2019t understand. Makes no sense to run a chronicle in a splat that I don\u2019t understand.<br /> <br /> What I <i>do</i> understand, and like a lot actually, are the monster powers. The three part dice pool is such a great mechanic imo because it separates the power rolls from regular skill rolls. I also love the way that they\u2019re divided into categories, or themes, because it makes sense that a power has multiple applications.\u200b Having some powers build off others makes perfect sense to me. Also many of the existing powers from VtR &amp; CtL, for example, work really really well for things I\u2019ve discussed w/ my players.<br /> <br /> But since these powers are for monster characters I can\u2019t use them as is for mortals. (I know some of you are saying &quot;just use Dread Powers&quot; \u2014 I tried. It\u2019s not gonna work.)<br /> <br /> For the time being this is what I\u2019ve been doing to rework these things\u2026<ul><li>First off the names are changed bc I have players that are used to playing other CofD &amp; WoD games &amp; things get confusing w/ all the similar names.</li> <li>The cost is switched to Willpower since humans don\u2019t have Vitae or Glamour.</li> <li>May or may not have certain caveats for higher level powers just so my players don\u2019t get too OP</li> </ul>My biggest issue is figuring out what to use instead of Blood Potency or Wyrd.<br /> <br /> This makes sense to me but that could just be because it\u2019s my idea. Anybody do this kind of thing before? Any advice, thoughts, comments, criticisms are appreciated.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27935-trynmybest","name":"trynmybest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27935_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-05T10:20:05-07:00","id":1510805,"title":"","content":"It seems you're doing a lot of work to reinvent the wheel here. You mention not understanding DtR, but wouldn't it be easier to learn that than to basically reinvent all the powers from all the different books? And you mention playing mortals, but you're not, you're playing vampire / changeling / whatever lite, still monsters just with more homebrew and less balance. <br /> <br /> So my first question is, what are your gains by doing it this way? Why do you want to do all of this work rather than sinking that same amount of work into a storyline and using regular mechanics? <br /> <br /> Second, are you concerned about artificially reducing the choices your players have by doing things in this manner? For example, if all the powers run off will power, every PC who wishes to have any kind of powers really needs a decent will power, which means having to take the stats that go into will power which limits the points available for other stats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-05T13:14:01-07:00","id":1510814,"title":"","content":"Ignoring Deviant, the way I would do this is to just write a new, more generic Supernatural Potency trait. You start with one dot for free, and it costs 5 Experience to raise like any other Potency trait. It would add to the activation roles of supernatural powers and supernatural resistance roles like normal, and also grants a supernatural Fuel pool, following the standard progression of other splats| (e.g. from 1 to five dots, it scales from 10 max and 1/round to 15 max and 5/round). You would then use this Fuel in place of Vitae/Glamour to power the re-fluffed Disciplines/Contracts.<br /> With this, you retain most of the mechanical balance. What it would lack is scaling drawbacks as your Potency increases, but adding those would require knowing more about the metaphysics/themes of the powers, and without any other features built in to the template to benefit from it, it shouldn't be big balance concern. The main problem is that you'd need to come up with a scheme for how points of Fuel are recovered. If you don't want to get too complicated, you could just set a rate of 1/chapter (or per scene if you want to up the power level). Maybe a 1-5 dot merit that recharges its rating in fuel at the start of each Chapter. There's also an opportunity to add a lot of flavor with the recharge method if you're so inclined.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't use willpower (exclusively at least) as the replacement for supernatural fuel. Things are balanced such that a point of willpower is normally worth more than a point of &quot;fuel&quot;, and normal splats get a pool 2+ times larger than an a typical willpower pool, with their own means of regaining points. If the characters are limited to willpower, the result will be powers that have to be used very sparingly, and implies they come at an emotional cost to the user. Normally willpower can only be recovered through rest and using Anchors. And each point spent on a power is one a character can't spend on &quot;normal&quot; stuff like adding dice to an important roll or resistance attribute. If you like the flavor of spending willpower on abilities, then I would suggest adding some kind of &quot;virtual&quot; willpower pool, that lets characters bank additional points that can only be spent on powers, via a merit or something.<br /> <br /> But really, what you describe sounds an awful lot like Deviant. Deviant does come with it's own complexity, in that theoretically every power has to be individually designed as a combination of a Variation (what the power does) and a Scar (the cost for using/having the power), but it's generally pretty easy to, say, slap a three-dot &quot;Costs Willpower to Activate&quot; Scar on something like &quot;Super Strength 3&quot; and call it good. And if you're not keen on some of the mechanical and thematic baggage that Deviant comes up, I wrote <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1470101-making-deviant-less-renagade-rules-hack\">some hacks</a> that strip it down to be more Chronicles-core friendly.<br /> <br /> Personally, I also like the way Disciplines are structured (particularly compared to &quot;bag of tricks&quot; type powers like Gifts). So I get the desire to maintain that structure without having to use the whole vampire package. If you really don't want to use Deviant, I think just using a striped down Supernatural Potency trait and Fuel pool should work well enough, especially if you're already willing to re-flavor everything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":23730,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","user":"Scriptorian","date":". 05-05-2023, 05:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-05T13:32:24-07:00","id":1510823,"title":"","content":"If DtR is too daunting, have you considered looking at Hurt Locker and the &quot;lesser&quot; templates? These are basically just small groups of otherwise normal people with access to a bunch of unique Merits that grant them various low-key powers. Many of them are also subtle enough that the characters themselves might not even realize that they're tapping into thing beyond normal human potential.<br /> <br /> It feels like it fits into the niche you're going for without having to do a lot of custom powers/etc.<br /> <br /> Though keep in mind that most supernaturals in the CofD have lesser templates as retainer-types as well. Ghouls, Wolf-Blooded, Proximi, etc. are all basically just humans with extra Merits. While many of them default towards being &quot;in the know&quot; there's plenty of space for them to come from a place of ignorance (esp. ones that can come from birth or at least don't require upkeep like Ghouls). A character could be a fae-touched due to a series of extravagant dreams that never resulted in one of the Gentry fully taking them to become a changeling for example, and they've never meet any of the Lost (yet) to understand how they've been changed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-05T19:00:42-07:00","id":1510847,"title":"","content":"I agree with what the others have suggested though to extend Scriptorian's point about Willpower you could take a look at the extra rules found in Hunter.<br /> <br /> Hunters have Touchstones which provide an extra source of Willpower and can risk Willpower on an action, getting back two if it succeeds, but suffering a Dramatic Failure if it fails.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27690-morgang","name":"MorganG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-05T20:57:46-07:00","id":1510853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1510760-reworking-monster-powers-for-cofd-blue-book-core?p=1510805#post1510805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems you're doing a lot of work to reinvent the wheel here. You mention not understanding DtR, but wouldn't it be easier to learn that than to basically reinvent all the powers from all the different books? And you mention playing mortals, but you're not, you're playing vampire / changeling / whatever lite, still monsters just with more homebrew and less balance.<br /> <br /> So my first question is, what are your gains by doing it this way? Why do you want to do all of this work rather than sinking that same amount of work into a storyline and using regular mechanics?<br /> <br /> Second, are you concerned about artificially reducing the choices your players have by doing things in this manner? For example, if all the powers run off will power, every PC who wishes to have any kind of powers really needs a decent will power, which means having to take the stats that go into will power which limits the points available for other stats.</div> </div> </div> </div>Idk if you\u2019re intending to come off as condescending but a lot of this comes across that way. But anyway I\u2019m not trying to reinvent all the powers from every single book. What I\u2019ve done is reworked a couple powers from a few books. It\u2019s not as extensive as you\u2019re making it sound.<br /> <br /> The goal (I think that\u2019s what you\u2019re meaning by &quot;gains&quot;) is pretty clear imo \u2014 in my understanding it seems perfectly possible to take a monster power &amp; give it to a human by switching out the power\u2019s monster stat for something humans have \u2014 and that\u2019s what I want to do. Not entirely sure what you mean by artificially reducing choices of my players so idk how to answer that.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d give an example of what I\u2019m doing but idk if it\u2019d help\u2026","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27935-trynmybest","name":"trynmybest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27935_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-05T21:29:27-07:00","id":1510856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1510760-reworking-monster-powers-for-cofd-blue-book-core?p=1510814#post1510814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't use willpower (exclusively at least) as the replacement for supernatural fuel. Things are balanced such that a point of willpower is normally worth more than a point of &quot;fuel&quot;, and normal splats get a pool 2+ times larger than an a typical willpower pool, with their own means of regaining points. If the characters are limited to willpower, the result will be powers that have to be used very sparingly, and implies they come at an emotional cost to the user. Normally willpower can only be recovered through rest and using Anchors. And each point spent on a power is one a character can't spend on &quot;normal&quot; stuff like adding dice to an important roll or resistance attribute.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I\u2019m not intending to only use willpower. Reason I put it in the post is simply because it was just the first thing I thought of while writing up what I\u2019ve done thus far \u2014 probably since the powers that I really want to use have a willpower cost. I didn\u2019t even think about how it would take away from normal willpower usage during play.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1510760-reworking-monster-powers-for-cofd-blue-book-core?p=1510814#post1510814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But really, what you describe sounds an awful lot like Deviant. Deviant does come with it's own complexity, in that theoretically every power has to be individually designed as a combination of a Variation (what the power does) and a Scar (the cost for using/having the power), but it's generally pretty easy to, say, slap a three-dot &quot;Costs Willpower to Activate&quot; Scar on something like &quot;Super Strength 3&quot; and call it good. And if you're not keen on some of the mechanical and thematic baggage that Deviant comes up, I wrote <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1470101-making-deviant-less-renagade-rules-hack\">some hacks</a> that strip it down to be more Chronicles-core friendly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I guess it does but in all honesty one of the things that turned me off of Deviant is the whole idea of Variations &amp; Scars. The way it\u2019s explained in the book confuses me &amp; makes it seem way more complicated than it should be imo. There\u2019s a lot of stuff in DtR that I like a lot, thematically speaking, it\u2019s the confusion on the mechanics &amp; a couple other elements. I will definitely look into those rules tho tysm!!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1510760-reworking-monster-powers-for-cofd-blue-book-core?p=1510814#post1510814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I also like the way Disciplines are structured (particularly compared to &quot;bag of tricks&quot; type powers like Gifts). So I get the desire to maintain that structure without having to use the whole vampire package. If you really don't want to use Deviant, I think just using a striped down Supernatural Potency trait and Fuel pool should work well enough, especially if you're already willing to re-flavor everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will definitely keep this idea in my back pocket just in case.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27935-trynmybest","name":"trynmybest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27935_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-05T21:33:20-07:00","id":1510857,"title":"","content":"That was not my intention. <br /> <br /> By gains I meant how is this making your game better than just playing the specific splats or dread powers or any of the ideas you discounted. What does this bring to your game that the easier options don't? <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-09T06:35:42-07:00","id":1511127,"title":"","content":"There's also the option, especially if you want more 'street level' powers, of just using Endowments from Hunter. Now admittedly the existing Endowments are narrow in theme and limited to certain groups, but there's no reason you have to keep to that. Hell put in a bit more backstory, a theme for their powers, and a loose goal and you already have a Conspiracy.<br /> <br /> There's also the option of just letting people take minor templates, both Wolf-Blooded and Fae Touched will work perfectly well outside of their 'communities', Wolf-Blooded can even hew closer to the common perception of werewolves with the right tells. Even the Hunter book minor template (Slashers) could work if a player is willing to work with you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}